{"name":"Tracery","hex":"#dbb9a0","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"tracery","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Bars or ribs, usually of stone or wood, or other material, that subdivide an opening or stand in relief against a door or wall as an ornamental feature.","A delicate interlacing of lines reminiscent of the architectural ornament."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tracery"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tracery","blocks":[{"text":"Tracery is an architectural device by which windows are divided into sections of various proportions by stone bars or ribs of moulding. Most commonly, it refers to the stonework elements that support the glass in a window. The purpose of the device is practical as well as decorative, because the increasingly large windows of Gothic buildings needed maximum support against the wind. The term probably derives from the tracing floors on which the complex patterns of windows were laid out in late Gothic architecture. Tracery can be found on the exterior of buildings as well as the interior."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Fenetre.cathedraleSoissons.png/330px-Fenetre.cathedraleSoissons.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tracery","wikidata":"Q847108"},{"title":"Tracery (horse)","blocks":[{"text":"Tracery (1909–1924) was an American-bred, British-trained Thoroughbred racehorse and sire, best known for winning the St. Leger Stakes in 1912. In a career which lasted from June 1912 until October 1913 he ran nine times and won six races. After finishing third on his debut in the 1912 Epsom Derby Tracery never lost another completed race at level weights. He won the St. James's Palace Stakes, Sussex Stakes and St. Leger Stakes in 1912 and the Eclipse Stakes and Champion Stakes as a four-year-old in 1913. He was brought down by a protester in the 1913 Ascot Gold Cup. After his retirement from racing he became a highly successful breeding stallion in Britain and Argentina."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b9/Tracery_at_1912_St_Leger_Stakes.png/330px-Tracery_at_1912_St_Leger_Stakes.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tracery_(horse)","wikidata":"Q17027108"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/Meneaux.fenetre.cathedrale.Reims.png/500px-Meneaux.fenetre.cathedrale.Reims.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/Meneaux.fenetre.cathedrale.Reims.png/500px-Meneaux.fenetre.cathedrale.Reims.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMeneaux.fenetre.cathedrale.Reims.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Laon_Cath%C3%A9drale_Notre-Dame_Nordrosette.jpg/500px-Laon_Cath%C3%A9drale_Notre-Dame_Nordrosette.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Laon_Cath%C3%A9drale_Notre-Dame_Nordrosette.jpg/1280px-Laon_Cath%C3%A9drale_Notre-Dame_Nordrosette.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Laon_Cath%C3%A9drale_Notre-Dame_Nordrosette.jpg/500px-Laon_Cath%C3%A9drale_Notre-Dame_Nordrosette.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Plate tracery, Laon Cathedral, north rose window","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALaon_Cath%C3%A9drale_Notre-Dame_Nordrosette.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/Lincoln_Cathedral%2C_Deans_eye_window_%2838137302184%29.jpg/500px-Lincoln_Cathedral%2C_Deans_eye_window_%2838137302184%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia